-- title:
--   Comparison of fundamental groups: Gal(K_U(k[X])/k(X)) is the geometric fundamental group of the affine line over F_q (EtPi1Geo library, file 03)
-- statement:
--   Library for comparing fundamental groups of curves over a finite field and over its algebraic closure. For a domain $A$ with fraction field $K$, $K_U \subset \overline{K}$ is the maximal extension of $K$ unramified over $A$ and $\pi_1 = \mathrm{Gal}(K_U/K)$ (Krull topology); for $K$ of characteristic $p$ and $q$ a power of $p$, $\pi_1^{\mathrm{geo}} \le \pi_1$ is the subgroup fixing every constant ($x^{q^n} = x$). Built on the flat curve library (`Def_RPLib_F2_032`). Contents:
--
--   * for a constant field extension $FK/F$ with algebraically closed constants, the field identification $\iota : K_U(A_K, FK) \cong K_U(A, F)$ (extending an $F$-embedding $FK \to \overline{F}$) and the comparison isomorphism of topological groups $\mathrm{cmp} : \pi_1(A_K, FK) \cong \pi_1^{\mathrm{geo}}(A, F)$, $\mathrm{cmp}(\sigma) = \iota \circ \sigma \circ \iota^{-1}$;
--   * the case of the affine line: for $k$ algebraically closed and algebraic over $\mathbb{F}_q$ and $FK = \mathrm{Frac}\, k[X]$, `cmpA1` : $\pi_1(k[X], FK) \cong \pi_1^{\mathrm{geo}}(\mathbb{F}_q[X], \mathbb{F}_q(X))$ with `cmpA1_apply`, the identification `iotaA1` restricting to the $\mathbb{F}_q(X)$-embedding on $FK$ (`iotaA1_algebraMap`, `iotaA1_X`), and `kA1_surj` (every constant is the image of an element of $k$).
-- source:
--   A. Grothendieck, Revêtements étales et groupe fondamental (SGA 1), Lecture Notes in Math. 224, Springer (1971), Exposés V and IX; J. S. Milne, Étale Cohomology, Princeton University Press (1980), Chapter I; J.-P. Serre, Local Fields, GTM 67, Springer (1979), Chapter I

